tations on the \"quieter digest\" feedback make it less actionable, as the legacy daily subscription issue would require restarting a terminated system. Mobile status filters are a concrete solution, with demonstrated desktop success. Therefore it's preferable to address this.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Mobile Filter Component**\n\nThe \"quieter digest\" is not the immediate priority, because its underlying notification-reset component has been terminated. Resurrecting this feature is outside the scope of the current work. Furthermore, the ticket's age is uncertain.\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\n**Recommending Mobile Status Filter Deployment**\n\nThe existing mobile component for status filters shows a path to reduce onboarding friction; desktop status filters now have solved performance bottlenecks (`current.md`). Desktop usage shows a 21% human weekly usage rate. The mobile implementation for status filter is the next logical step to replicate success.\n\nInvestigating `history/support/record-0131162d69.md` revealed initial performance issues for the Focus Shelf feature, but the architectural fix from August addressed the performance bottlenecks. The \"quieter digest\" feedback is less actionable, given the limitations in legacy subscriptions.\n\nDeployment for this week can begin, given the existing mobile component. The uncertainty lies in mobile performance on larger workspaces, mobile draft component readiness/testing across iOS/Android, and also the unknown submission date of ticket `record-5f1a34c149`.\n\nRecommend mobile status filter deployment.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"grep -E \"(Submitted|Retrieved|Dated):\" /workspace/product/history/support/*.md","Cwd":"/workspace","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Check dates in all history/support files"}}]}
